From: RK3128 reference <frame@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer eligible 2.4 GHz BSSes unless Settings enables 5 GHz

Keep normal security, ignore-list, priority and BSSID checks. Run their
2.4 GHz candidates first; fall back to the original all-band search when
none is usable. No permanent scan restriction or fallback timer is needed. The separate
/data/state/wifi/band policy defaults OFF and is written by the root launcher
helper. Old images ignore it: never put a new keyword into the saved network
configuration, or rollback to the previous supplicant would lose Wi-Fi.
The runtime rk3128_wifi5 SET/STATUS field changes without a daemon restart.
ON retains upstream choice (#499). Reconnect hints must not hide the other band: only
use a previous 2.4 GHz channel while OFF, or a previous 5 GHz channel while ON.

--- a/wpa_supplicant/config.h
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/config.h
@@ -943,6 +943,10 @@
 	 */
 	int *freq_list;
 
+	/* RK3128 reference: 0 prefers eligible 2.4 GHz BSSes, 1 keeps both bands.
+	 * The separate /data policy defaults OFF; network configs stay compatible. */
+	int rk3128_wifi5;
+
 	/**
 	 * initial_freq_list - like freq_list but for initial scan
 	 *
--- a/wpa_supplicant/config.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/config.c
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
